(* Variant quic-cert: the session handshake over QUIC, as the code has it, against an attacker that holds the key of the
   certificate of the server (AUD-5, #389; AUD-6, #409; CORE-H5, #408). The binding is the TLS exporter of the QUIC
   connection (TransportQuicExporter), so the middlebox that presents the pinned certificate to the client and opens a
   session of its own to the server has another exporter on each side, and the handshake that it relays does not
   complete: finding F1, which the tls-server-end-point of the build before CORE-H5 had (endpoint-cert), is closed. *)

process
  ( Setup()
  | LeakCertServer()
  | Sessions(pin_on, bt_export, bt_export, kp_on, plabel_session, lab_exp_session, suite_hfs)
  )
